      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean i get that there isn't an official study on it yet but the timing is just too perfect. i've been a professional artist for 15 years and this drop in cognitive flow is unlike anything else. it feels intentional, like a subtle layer of interference. if we can't find a study, can we at least look at the physics of it? like, what kind of copper mesh or electromagnetic shielding would be most effective at blocking high-frequency signals in a dedicated workspace?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
