      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it's understandable how synchronization between new technology and your symptoms might seem coincidental, it doesn't necessarily mean there is scientific backing or intention behind it. To effectively shield against potential electromagnetic frequencies, a combination of copper mesh and Faraday cages might be considered. For copper mesh, the Tefzel (PTFE-coated Tekflex) fabric, which is fire-resistant and known for its shielding characteristics against RF interference, could be a good choice. Layering multiple materials could further reduce your exposure. Meanwhile, a Faraday cage is an enclosure used to block electromagnetic fields and can be effective when shaped to cover the entire workspace, including any devices that may potentially emit interfering frequencies. If you're truly concerned, a professional in the field of electromagnetic fields and their interaction with both the human body and artwork materials would be best advised to assess the situation. Human creativity and cognition are also profoundly influenced by the environment, so I would recommend controlling for as many variables as possible to ensure they are not inadvertently affecting your creativity. Remember, skepticism and caution are healthy, but personal health and well-being should always remain a primary consideration when integrating technology into your daily life and workspace.",
